<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cb53a56ccc6a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Stanford Medicine leadership has since apologized and promised to re-evaluate the plan." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1530" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f119c8b07091> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The algorithm’s third category refers to the California Department of Public Health’s vaccine allocation guidelines." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1588" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/69baea65a0ad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Mass General Brigham in Boston categorizes employees into four groups based on department and job location, according to an internal email reviewed by MIT Technology Review." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1588" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9a09d8361448> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An algorithm determining which Stanford Medicine employees would receive its 5,000 initial doses of the COVID-19 vaccine included just seven medical residents / fellows on the list, according to a December 17th letter sent from Stanford Medicine’s chief resident council.",
        "An algorithm determining which Stanford Medicine employees would receive its 5,000 initial doses of the COVID-19 vaccine included just seven medical residents / fellows on the list." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1530" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9e543c395c55> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Nuriel Moghavem, a neurology resident who was the first to publicize the problems at Stanford, tweeted on Friday afternoon that he had finally received his vaccine—not at Stanford, but at a public county hospital in Santa Clara County." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1588" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d9e02a4d62f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Stanford Medicine residents who work in close contact with COVID-19 patients were left out of the first wave of staff members for the new Pfizer vaccine." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1205" .

